/given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endoscopic release of limb constriction rings in utero</article-title><source>Fetal Diagn Ther</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16601333</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quintero</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Morales</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalter</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Angel</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In utero lysis of amniotic bands</article-title><source>Ultrasound Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1997</year><volume>10</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>316</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9444044</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keswani</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Adzick</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>In utero limb salvage: fetoscopic release of amniotic bands for threatened limb amputation</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>38</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>848</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12778379</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Constriction ring with persistent fibrous band at the distal aspect of the right leg.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e4_fig1"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>(a) Right leg after fibrous band is cut. (b) Persistent fibrous band.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e4_fig2"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Comparison of affected and unaffected legs.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e4_fig3"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>One-year following birth. (a) Plantar flexion and (b) dorsiflexion.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e4_fig4"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>